{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol | sed -n '1,360p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol | sed -n '170,360p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\tpragma solidity 0.8.36;\n     3\t\n     4\timport { Clones } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol\";\n     5\timport { IERC20Metadata } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/IERC20Metadata.sol\";\n     6\timport { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n     7\timport { ReentrancyGuard } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n     8\timport { IERC165 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/introspection/IERC165.sol\";\n     9\t\n    10\timport { Raffle } from \"./Raffle.sol\";\n    11\timport { IRaffle } from \"./interfaces/IRaffle.sol\";\n    12\timport { IRaffleFactory } from \"./interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol\";\n    13\timport { RaffleConstants } from \"./libraries/RaffleConstants.sol\";\n    14\t\n    15\t/// @title raffle.fun Canonical USDC Raffle Factory\n    16\t/// @author heesho\n    17\t/// @notice Atomically creates, funds, and registers autonomous fixed-implementation raffle clones.\n    18\t/// @dev The implementation, canonical six-decimal USDC, treasury, fee, and Chainlink configuration are immutable. The\n    19\t///      factory has no owner, pause, upgrade, rescue, or mutable protocol configuration.\n    20\t/// @custom:version 1.0.0\n    21\tcontract RaffleFactory is IRaffleFactory, ReentrancyGuard {\n    22\t    // Constants\n    23\t\n    24\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    25\t    uint32 public constant override callbackGasLimit = RaffleConstants.VRF_CALLBACK_GAS_LIMIT;\n    26\t\n    27\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    28\t    uint16 public constant override requestConfirmations = RaffleConstants.VRF_REQUEST_CONFIRMATIONS;\n    29\t\n    30\t    // Immutables and state\n    31\t\n    32\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    33\t    address public immutable override quoteToken;\n    34\t\n    35\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    36\t    address public immutable override vrfWrapper;\n    37\t\n    38\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    39\t    address public immutable override protocolTreasury;\n    40\t\n    41\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    42\t    address public immutable override raffleImplementation;\n    43\t\n    44\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    45\t    uint256 public override raffleCount;\n    46\t\n    47\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    48\t    mapping(uint256 raffleId => address raffle) public override raffleById;\n    49\t\n    50\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    51\t    mapping(address raffle => uint256 raffleId) public override idByRaffle;\n    52\t\n    53\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    54\t    mapping(address raffle => bool registered) public override isRaffle;\n    55\t\n    56\t    // Constructor\n    57\t\n    58\t    /// @notice Deploys the ownerless factory and its locked raffle implementation with one immutable configuration.\n    59\t    /// @dev The quote token must report exactly six decimals; the wrapper and quote token must contain deployed code.\n    60\t    ///      Deployment tooling must supply and verify the target chain's official USDC address because the constructor\n    61\t    ///      cannot prove token identity from metadata.\n    62\t    /// @param quoteToken_ Target chain's official six-decimal USDC contract trusted by every raffle.\n    63\t    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Official Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper for the target chain.\n    64\t    /// @param protocolTreasury_ Immutable protocol-fee recipient used by every raffle.\n    65\t    constructor(address quoteToken_, address vrfWrapper_, address protocolTreasury_) {\n    66\t        _requireContract(quoteToken_);\n    67\t        _requireContract(vrfWrapper_);\n    68\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n    69\t\n    70\t        uint8 quoteDecimals = 0;\n    71\t        try IERC20Metadata(quoteToken_).decimals() returns (uint8 decimals_) {\n    72\t            quoteDecimals = decimals_;\n    73\t        } catch {\n    74\t            revert UnsupportedQuoteToken(quoteToken_);\n    75\t        }\n    76\t        if (quoteDecimals != RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS) {\n    77\t            revert InvalidQuoteTokenDecimals(quoteDecimals, RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS);\n    78\t        }\n    79\t\n    80\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(this) || protocolTreasury_ == quoteToken_ || protocolTreasury_ == vrfWrapper_)\n    81\t        {\n    82\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    83\t        }\n    84\t\n    85\t        quoteToken = quoteToken_;\n    86\t        vrfWrapper = vrfWrapper_;\n    87\t        protocolTreasury = protocolTreasury_;\n    88\t\n    89\t        address implementation = address(new Raffle(quoteToken_, vrfWrapper_));\n    90\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == implementation) revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    91\t        raffleImplementation = implementation;\n    92\t    }\n    93\t\n    94\t    // External state-changing functions\n    95\t\n    96\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    97\t    function createRaffle(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) external override nonReentrant returns (address raffle) {\n    98\t        _validateCreateParams(params);\n    99\t        uint256 currentTime = block.timestamp;\n   100\t        if (params.endTime <= currentTime) revert InvalidEndTime(currentTime, params.endTime);\n   101\t        uint256 saleDuration = uint256(params.endTime) - currentTime;\n   102\t        if (saleDuration > RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION) {\n   103\t            revert SaleDurationTooLong(saleDuration, RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION);\n   104\t        }\n   105\t        uint256 raffleId = ++raffleCount;\n   106\t        raffle = Clones.clone(raffleImplementation);\n   107\t        // The fresh fixed-target clone can initialize only once; this function is nonReentrant and atomic.\n   108\t        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-no-eth\n   109\t        IRaffle(raffle)\n   110\t            .initialize(\n   111\t                IRaffle.RaffleInitParams({\n   112\t                sponsor: msg.sender,\n   113\t                sponsorRecipient: params.sponsorRecipient,\n   114\t                protocolTreasury: protocolTreasury,\n   115\t                prizeToken: params.prizeToken,\n   116\t                prizeTokenId: params.prizeTokenId,\n   117\t                raffleId: raffleId,\n   118\t                reserveEntries: params.reserveEntries,\n   119\t                endTime: params.endTime\n   120\t            })\n   121\t            );\n   122\t\n   123\t        raffleById[raffleId] = raffle;\n   124\t        idByRaffle[raffle] = raffleId;\n   125\t        isRaffle[raffle] = true;\n   126\t\n   127\t        IERC721 prize = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\n   128\t        prize.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, raffle, params.prizeTokenId);\n   129\t        if (prize.ownerOf(params.prizeTokenId) != raffle) {\n   130\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   131\t        }\n   132\t        if (IRaffle(raffle).status() != IRaffle.Status.Active) {\n   133\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   134\t        }\n   135\t\n   136\t        emit RaffleCreated(\n   137\t            raffleId,\n   138\t            raffle,\n   139\t            msg.sender,\n   140\t            params.sponsorRecipient,\n   141\t            params.prizeToken,\n   142\t            params.prizeTokenId,\n   143\t            quoteToken,\n   144\t            protocolTreasury,\n   145\t            params.reserveEntries,\n   146\t            params.endTime\n   147\t        );\n   148\t    }\n   149\t\n   150\t    // Private view helpers\n   151\t\n   152\t    /// @dev Validates the sponsor-selected token, recipient, reserve, and supported ERC-721 interface before cloning.\n   153\t    /// @param params Prospective raffle configuration supplied by the sponsor.\n   154\t    function _validateCreateParams(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) private view {\n   155\t        _requireContract(params.prizeToken);\n   156\t        if (params.sponsorRecipient == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n   157\t        if (\n   158\t            params.prizeToken == address(this) || params.prizeToken == quoteToken || params.prizeToken == vrfWrapper\n   159\t                || params.prizeToken == raffleImplementation || isRaffle[params.prizeToken]\n   160\t        ) {\n   161\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.prizeToken);\n   162\t        }\n   163\t        if (\n   164\t            params.sponsorRecipient == address(this) || params.sponsorRecipient == quoteToken\n   165\t                || params.sponsorRecipient == vrfWrapper || params.sponsorRecipient == params.prizeToken\n   166\t                || params.sponsorRecipient == raffleImplementation || isRaffle[params.sponsorRecipient]\n   167\t        ) {\n   168\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.sponsorRecipient);\n   169\t        }\n   170\t\n   171\t        bool supports721 = false;\n   172\t        try IERC165(params.prizeToken).supportsInterface(type(IERC721).interfaceId) returns (bool supported) {\n   173\t            supports721 = supported;\n   174\t        } catch {\n   175\t            revert UnsupportedPrizeToken(params.prizeToken);\n   176\t        }\n   177\t        if (!supports721) revert UnsupportedPrizeToken(params.prizeToken);\n   178\t        if (params.reserveEntries == 0) revert ZeroReserveEntries();\n   179\t    }\n   180\t\n   181\t    /// @dev Reverts unless an address contains deployed code.\n   182\t    /// @param account Address required to be a contract.\n   183\t    function _requireContract(address account) private view {\n   184\t        if (account.code.length == 0) revert NotContract(account);\n   185\t    }\n   186\t}\n   170\t    /**\n   171\t     * @dev Checks if `spender` can operate on `tokenId`, assuming the provided `owner` is the actual owner.\n   172\t     * Reverts if:\n   173\t     * - `spender` does not have approval from `owner` for `tokenId`.\n   174\t     * - `spender` does not have approval to manage all of `owner`'s assets.\n   175\t     *\n   176\t     * WARNING: This function assumes that `owner` is the actual owner of `tokenId` and does not verify this\n   177\t     * assumption.\n   178\t     */\n   179\t    function _checkAuthorized(address owner, address spender, uint256 tokenId) internal view virtual {\n   180\t        if (!_isAuthorized(owner, spender, tokenId)) {\n   181\t            if (owner == address(0)) {\n   182\t                revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   183\t            } else {\n   184\t                revert ERC721InsufficientApproval(spender, tokenId);\n   185\t            }\n   186\t        }\n   187\t    }\n   188\t\n   189\t    /**\n   190\t     * @dev Unsafe write access to the balances, used by extensions that \"mint\" tokens using an {ownerOf} override.\n   191\t     *\n   192\t     * NOTE: the value is limited to type(uint128).max. This protect against _balance overflow. It is unrealistic that\n   193\t     * a uint256 would ever overflow from increments when these increments are bounded to uint128 values.\n   194\t     *\n   195\t     * WARNING: Increasing an account's balance using this function tends to be paired with an override of the\n   196\t     * {_ownerOf} function to resolve the ownership of the corresponding tokens so that balances and ownership\n   197\t     * remain consistent with one another.\n   198\t     */\n   199\t    function _increaseBalance(address account, uint128 value) internal virtual {\n   200\t        unchecked {\n   201\t            _balances[account] += value;\n   202\t        }\n   203\t    }\n   204\t\n   205\t    /**\n   206\t     * @dev Transfers `tokenId` from its current owner to `to`, or alternatively mints (or burns) if the current owner\n   207\t     * (or `to`) is the zero address. Returns the owner of the `tokenId` before the update.\n   208\t     *\n   209\t     * The `auth` argument is optional. If the value passed is non 0, then this function will check that\n   210\t     * `auth` is either the owner of the token, or approved to operate on the token (by the owner).\n   211\t     *\n   212\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   213\t     *\n   214\t     * NOTE: If overriding this function in a way that tracks balances, see also {_increaseBalance}.\n   215\t     */\n   216\t    function _update(address to, uint256 tokenId, address auth) internal virtual returns (address) {\n   217\t        address from = _ownerOf(tokenId);\n   218\t\n   219\t        // Perform (optional) operator check\n   220\t        if (auth != address(0)) {\n   221\t            _checkAuthorized(from, auth, tokenId);\n   222\t        }\n   223\t\n   224\t        // Execute the update\n   225\t        if (from != address(0)) {\n   226\t            // Clear approval. No need to re-authorize or emit the Approval event\n   227\t            _approve(address(0), tokenId, address(0), false);\n   228\t\n   229\t            unchecked {\n   230\t                _balances[from] -= 1;\n   231\t            }\n   232\t        }\n   233\t\n   234\t        if (to != address(0)) {\n   235\t            unchecked {\n   236\t                _balances[to] += 1;\n   237\t            }\n   238\t        }\n   239\t\n   240\t        _owners[tokenId] = to;\n   241\t\n   242\t        emit Transfer(from, to, tokenId);\n   243\t\n   244\t        return from;\n   245\t    }\n   246\t\n   247\t    /**\n   248\t     * @dev Mints `tokenId` and transfers it to `to`.\n   249\t     *\n   250\t     * WARNING: Usage of this method is discouraged, use {_safeMint} whenever possible\n   251\t     *\n   252\t     * Requirements:\n   253\t     *\n   254\t     * - `tokenId` must not exist.\n   255\t     * - `to` cannot be the zero address.\n   256\t     *\n   257\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   258\t     */\n   259\t    function _mint(address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   260\t        if (to == address(0)) {\n   261\t            revert ERC721InvalidReceiver(address(0));\n   262\t        }\n   263\t        address previousOwner = _update(to, tokenId, address(0));\n   264\t        if (previousOwner != address(0)) {\n   265\t            revert ERC721InvalidSender(address(0));\n   266\t        }\n   267\t    }\n   268\t\n   269\t    /**\n   270\t     * @dev Mints `tokenId`, transfers it to `to` and checks for `to` acceptance.\n   271\t     *\n   272\t     * Requirements:\n   273\t     *\n   274\t     * - `tokenId` must not exist.\n   275\t     * - If `to` refers to a smart contract, it must implement {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received}, which is called upon a safe transfer.\n   276\t     *\n   277\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   278\t     */\n   279\t    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   280\t        _safeMint(to, tokenId, \"\");\n   281\t    }\n   282\t\n   283\t    /**\n   284\t     * @dev Same as {xref-ERC721-_safeMint-address-uint256-}[`_safeMint`], with an additional `data` parameter which is\n   285\t     * forwarded in {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} to contract recipients.\n   286\t     */\n   287\t    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal virtual {\n   288\t        _mint(to, tokenId);\n   289\t        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), address(0), to, tokenId, data);\n   290\t    }\n   291\t\n   292\t    /**\n   293\t     * @dev Destroys `tokenId`.\n   294\t     * The approval is cleared when the token is burned.\n   295\t     * This is an internal function that does not check if the sender is authorized to operate on the token.\n   296\t     *\n   297\t     * Requirements:\n   298\t     *\n   299\t     * - `tokenId` must exist.\n   300\t     *\n   301\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   302\t     */\n   303\t    function _burn(uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   304\t        address previousOwner = _update(address(0), tokenId, address(0));\n   305\t        if (previousOwner == address(0)) {\n   306\t            revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   307\t        }\n   308\t    }\n   309\t\n   310\t    /**\n   311\t     * @dev Transfers `tokenId` from `from` to `to`.\n   312\t     *  As opposed to {transferFrom}, this imposes no restrictions on msg.sender.\n   313\t     *\n   314\t     * Requirements:\n   315\t     *\n   316\t     * - `to` cannot be the zero address.\n   317\t     * - `tokenId` token must be owned by `from`.\n   318\t     *\n   319\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   320\t     */\n   321\t    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   322\t        if (to == address(0)) {\n   323\t            revert ERC721InvalidReceiver(address(0));\n   324\t        }\n   325\t        address previousOwner = _update(to, tokenId, address(0));\n   326\t        if (previousOwner == address(0)) {\n   327\t            revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   328\t        } else if (previousOwner != from) {\n   329\t            revert ERC721IncorrectOwner(from, tokenId, previousOwner);\n   330\t        }\n   331\t    }\n   332\t\n   333\t    /**\n   334\t     * @dev Safely transfers `tokenId` token from `from` to `to`, checking that contract recipients\n   335\t     * are aware of the ERC-721 standard to prevent tokens from being forever locked.\n   336\t     *\n   337\t     * `data` is additional data, it has no specified format and it is sent in call to `to`.\n   338\t     *\n   339\t     * This internal function is like {safeTransferFrom} in the sense that it invokes\n   340\t     * {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} on the receiver, and can be used to e.g.\n   341\t     * implement alternative mechanisms to perform token transfer, such as signature-based.\n   342\t     *\n   343\t     * Requirements:\n   344\t     *\n   345\t     * - `tokenId` token must exist and be owned by `from`.\n   346\t     * - `to` cannot be the zero address.\n   347\t     * - `from` cannot be the zero address.\n   348\t     * - If `to` refers to a smart contract, it must implement {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received}, which is called upon a safe transfer.\n   349\t     *\n   350\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   351\t     */\n   352\t    function _safeTransfer(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   353\t        _safeTransfer(from, to, tokenId, \"\");\n   354\t    }\n   355\t\n   356\t    /**\n   357\t     * @dev Same as {xref-ERC721-_safeTransfer-address-address-uint256-}[`_safeTransfer`], with an additional `data` parameter which is\n   358\t     * forwarded in {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} to contract recipients.\n   359\t     */\n   360\t    function _safeTransfer(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal virtual {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"A nested invocation is rejected by the inherited reentrancy guard before the caller-controlled candidate ticket reaches settlement logic.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - receives the ABI-decoded ticketId on the permissionless external entrypoint and applies nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 ReentrancyGuard.nonReentrant - invokes the pre-entry guard before dispatching the function body.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - detects an already-entered guard state.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:90 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - reverts with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall().\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall(); the settlement body is not entered and all enclosing transaction effects revert if the error is not caught.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":304,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller supplies ticketId in the external calldata, but the guard rejects the nested call before line 305 forwards or reads that value.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the entrypoint's reentrancy boundary. It prevents callbacks occurring during another guarded Raffle operation from entering settlement against intermediate state.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A call made after terminal liabilities have already been allocated is rejected before status or ticket-range validation, preserving one-shot settlement.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - accepts the caller-controlled ticketId under the nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - verifies the call is not nested and marks the guard entered.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - forwards ticketId unchanged to _settleWinningTicket.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:533 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - enters the shared private settlement routine.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - observes settlementComplete and reverts with SettlementAlreadyComplete().\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with SettlementAlreadyComplete(); no status, range, liability, or winning-ticket state is changed.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":534,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled ticketId reaches _settleWinningTicket but is not read or used because settlementComplete is checked first.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The one-shot gate prevents a subsequent permissionless caller from replacing winningTicketId or reallocating the already-created winner, sponsor, and protocol claims.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A call while the raffle is not in either resolved result state is rejected before the candidate ticket is looked up.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - receives the caller-controlled ticketId under the nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - forwards ticketId unchanged to _settleWinningTicket.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - confirms settlement has not already completed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:535 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - loads the current raffle status.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:536 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - requires exactly NftWon or CashWon and otherwise reverts with InvalidStatus(result).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with InvalidStatus(currentStatus); no ticket mapping is read and no accounting state is mutated.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":536,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled ticketId is forwarded into the helper but remains unused when the lifecycle-status validation fails.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This lifecycle boundary prevents settlement before an authenticated draw has selected winningEntry and fixed the NftWon or CashWon result, and also excludes the Refunding branch.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"In a resolved, unsettled raffle, a losing or never-minted candidate ticket is rejected because its stored inclusive range does not contain winningEntry.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - receives the caller-controlled candidate ticketId under the nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - forwards the same ticketId to _settleWinningTicket.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - passes the one-shot settlement check.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:535 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - passes the NftWon/CashWon status check.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:538 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - dispatches ticketId to _requireWinningTicket without checking caller identity or ticket ownership.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:580 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - passes ticketId to ticketRange.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:451 Raffle.ticketRange - uses ticketId as the _ticketRanges mapping key and loads firstEntry and lastEntry; an unknown ID yields zero values.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:581 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - loads the authenticated winningEntry selected during resolution.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:582 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - compares winningEntry with the candidate's inclusive range.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:583 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - reverts with TicketDoesNotContainWinningEntry(ticketId, selectedEntry) when the range proof fails.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with TicketDoesNotContainWinningEntry(candidateTicketId, winningEntry); no liabilities are allocated.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":582,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled ticketId becomes the _ticketRanges mapping key and is included in the custom-error data when its loaded range excludes winningEntry.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This comparison is the sole winner-proof boundary on a permissionless, ownership-independent settlement call; it prevents an arbitrary candidate ID from becoming the canonical winning ticket.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an unsettled NftWon raffle and a candidate whose stored range contains winningEntry, permissionless settlement records the canonical winning ticket, allocates the pot between sponsor and protocol claims, emits the result, and returns zero without transferring an asset.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - receives ticketId and enters through the nonReentrant boundary; no caller authorization is required.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - forwards ticketId unchanged to _settleWinningTicket.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - verifies settlement is not complete.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:535 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - loads the NftWon result.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:538 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - requires the supplied ticket's stored range to contain winningEntry.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:580 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - resolves _ticketRanges[ticketId] through ticketRange and accepts the inclusive-range proof.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:539 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - snapshots unsettledPot as grossPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:540 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - calculates the protocol fee with floor division at PROTOCOL_FEE_BPS/BPS.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:543 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - dispatches through the NftWon economic branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:544 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - allocates grossPot minus protocolFee to sponsorProceeds; cashAmount remains zero.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:551 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - marks settlementComplete true.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:552 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the proven caller-supplied ticketId as winningTicketId.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:553 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - zeros unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:554 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the sponsor claim.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:555 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the protocol-fee claim.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:557 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - emits WinningTicketSettled with ticketId, msg.sender, NftWon, zero cash, and both allocations.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - restores the guard after successful execution.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - returns cashAmount equal to zero.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Atomically commit winningTicketId and terminal sponsor/protocol liabilities, clear unsettledPot, emit WinningTicketSettled, and return 0; no ERC-20 or ERC-721 external call occurs.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":543,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"After ticketId indexes _ticketRanges and passes the winning-entry proof, that same unmodified value is persisted as winningTicketId and indexed in WinningTicketSettled. It does not select a recipient or amount, and ownership is deliberately not read.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This branch permanently identifies the transferable bearer ticket entitled to later NFT redemption and converts the full pot into sponsor and protocol claims. Its permissionless proof, economic allocation, and one-shot state transition are security-critical.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an unsettled CashWon raffle and a candidate whose stored range contains winningEntry, permissionless settlement records the canonical winning ticket, allocates cash-winner, sponsor, and protocol claims, emits the result, and returns the allocated cash amount without transferring tokens.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:304 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - receives ticketId and enters through the nonReentrant boundary; no caller authorization is required.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - forwards ticketId unchanged to _settleWinningTicket.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:534 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - verifies settlement is not complete.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:535 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - loads the CashWon result.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:538 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - requires the supplied ticket's stored range to contain winningEntry.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:580 Raffle._requireWinningTicket - resolves _ticketRanges[ticketId] through ticketRange and accepts the inclusive-range proof.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:539 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - snapshots unsettledPot as grossPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:540 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - calculates the protocol fee with floor division at PROTOCOL_FEE_BPS/BPS.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:546 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - calculates cashAmount with floor division at CASH_WINNER_BPS/BPS.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:547 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - assigns the residual grossPot minus protocol fee and winner allocation to the sponsor.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:548 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores cashAmount in winnerProceeds for later owner redemption.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:551 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - marks settlementComplete true.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:552 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the proven caller-supplied ticketId as winningTicketId.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:553 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - zeros unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:554 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the sponsor claim.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:555 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - stores the protocol-fee claim.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:557 Raffle._settleWinningTicket - emits WinningTicketSettled with ticketId, msg.sender, CashWon, and all allocations.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - restores the guard after successful execution.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:305 Raffle.settleWinningTicket - returns the allocated cashAmount.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Atomically commit winningTicketId and winner/sponsor/protocol liabilities, clear unsettledPot, emit WinningTicketSettled, and return the cash allocation; no ERC-20 transfer occurs during settlement.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":546,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"After ticketId indexes _ticketRanges and passes the winning-entry proof, the same unmodified value is persisted as winningTicketId and indexed in WinningTicketSettled. It identifies the later bearer claim but does not choose the payout address or calculate the amounts.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This branch partitions the escrowed pot into the cash winner's claim, sponsor proceeds, and protocol fees while permanently binding redemption to the validated caller-selected ticket ID. The proof and accounting transition therefore warrant security review.\"}]}"}}
